<title>SPAIN: Spain had 55.2 bln pta Oct budget deficit - EconMin.</title>
<headline>Spain had 55.2 bln pta Oct budget deficit - EconMin.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economy Ministry gave the following breakdown of figures in billions of pesetas:</p>
<p> BUDGET OPERATIONS	    OCT 96	SEPT 96	  OCT 95</p>
<p> Revenues			1,531.7	 945.3	  1,580.8</p>
<p> Expenditure		   1,586.9     1,138.7	  1,338.8</p>
<p> Deficit/surplus		 -55.2	-193.4	    242.0</p>
<p> Def/surplus to date	-2,236.0    -2,180.8	 -2,271.2</p>
<p> GBR yr to date		3,419.7     2,668.3	  2,858.6</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures relate to central government finances only. GBR = government borrowing requirement.</p>
<p>The accumulated deficit to September was revised to 2,180.8 billion pesetas from 2,180.4 due to a technical adjustment by the Economy Ministry.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
